div.p:
thence the old boundary between Germany and Austria, then the old boundary
                    between Germany and Russia to its junction with the administrative boundary
                    between Posnania and Upper Silesia;

a line to be fixed on the ground passing west of Hennersdorf, Polkowitz, Noldau,
                    Steinersdorf and Dammer, and east of Strehlitz, Nassadel, Eckersdorf, Schwirz
                    and Städtel;
